  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَالشَّمْسِ وَضُحٰٮهَاۙ‏(1)\nWASH SHAMSE WA ZOHAAHAA.\nBy the Sun and his (glorious) splendour; \nوَالْقَمَرِ اِذَا تَلٰٮهَا  ۙ‏(2)\nWAL QAMARE EZAA TALAAHAA.\nBy the Moon as she follows him; \nوَالنَّهَارِ اِذَا جَلّٰٮهَا ۙ‏(3)\nWAN NAHAARE EZAA JALLAAHAA.\nBy the Day as it shows up (the Sun's) glory; \nوَالَّيْلِ اِذَا يَغْشٰٮهَا ۙ‏(4)\nWAL LAYLE EZAA YAGHSHAAHAA.\nBy the Night as it conceals it; \nوَالسَّمَآءِ وَمَا بَنٰٮهَا ۙ‏(5)\nWAS SAMAAA-E WA MAA BANAAHAA.\nBy the Firmament and its (wonderful) structure; \nوَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا طَحٰٮهَا ۙ‏(6)\nWAL ARZE WA MAA TAHAAHAA.\nBy the Earth and its (wide) expanse: \nوَنَفْسٍ وَّمَا سَوّٰٮهَا ۙ‏(7)\nWA NAFSINW WA MAA SAWWAAHAA.\nBy the Soul, and the proportion and order given to it; \nفَاَلْهَمَهَا فُجُوْرَهَا وَتَقْوٰٮهَا ۙ‏(8)\nFA-ALHAMAHAA FOJOORAHAA WA TAQWAAHAA.\nAnd its enlightenment as to its wrong and its right;- \nقَدْ اَفْلَحَ مَنْ زَكّٰٮهَا ۙ‏(9)\nQAD AFLAHA MAN ZAKKAAHAA.\nTruly he succeeds that purifies it, \nوَقَدْ خَابَ مَنْ دَسّٰٮهَا ؕ‏(10)\nWA QAD KHAABA MAN DASSAAHAA.\nAnd he fails that corrupts it! \nكَذَّبَتْ ثَمُوْدُ بِطَغْوٰٮهَآ  ۙ‏(11)\nKAZZABAT SAMOODO BE-TAGHWAAHAA.\nThe Thamud (people) rejected (their prophet) through their inordinate wrong-doing, \nاِذِ انْۢبَعَثَ اَشْقٰٮهَا  ۙ‏(12)\nEZIM BA-A’SA ASHQAAHAA.\nBehold, the most wicked man among them was deputed (for impiety). \nفَقَالَ لَهُمْ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ نَاقَةَ اللّٰهِ وَسُقْيٰهَا ؕ‏(13)\nFAQAALA LAHUM RASOOLUL LAAHE NAAQATAL LAAHE WA SUQYAAHAA.\nBut the Messenger of Allah said to them: “It is a She-camel of Allah! And (bar her not from) having her drink!” \nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَعَقَرُوْهَا  ۙفَدَمْدَمَ عَلَيْهِمْ رَبُّهُمْ بِذَنْۢبِهِمْ فَسَوّٰٮهَا  ۙ‏(14)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FA-A’QAROOHAA, FA-DAMDAMA A’LAYHIM RABBOHUM BE-ZAMBEHIM FASAWWAAHAA.\nThen they rejected him (as a false prophet), and they hamstrung her. So their Lord, on account of their crime, obliterated their traces and made them equal (in destruction, high and low)! \nوَلَا يَخَافُ عُقْبٰهَا‏(15)\nWA LAA YAKHAAFO UQBAAHAA.\nAnd for Him is no fear of its consequences. ",
  "merits": "This is a ‘Makki’ Surah and has 15 verse. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (S) that the reward for reciting this Surah is compared to the things upon which the sun and the moon shine.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that the person who recites Surah as-Shams, al-Layl, az-Zoha and al-Insherah will, on the Day of Judgement, find all creatures of the earth testifying on his behalf and Allah will accept their testimony and give him a place in Jannah. Recitation of this Surah also leads to an increase in sustenance, courage and popularity amongst the people."
